  "note": "THES STAFF ROSTER is a four-sub-column table: left name (x=39) / left title (x=68) / right name (x=98) / right TEAM COLOR (x=131-140). The schema has no colour field, so the printed Team Color for each grade-level teacher is recorded here: Grade 3 - Quinn Cavaco Red, Amy Harrington Red, Nancy Murray Blue, Rich Bowen Blue, Erin Gyles White. Grade 4 - Erin Blanchette Blue, Danielle Celona Blue, Gina Cote White, Charlotte Guinto Red, Lynn Marabello Red. Grade 5 - Narci Woods Red, Brian Chartrand White, Rhonda Connery White, Kate Robinson Blue, Heather Witham Blue. No role is printed for those teachers (the second right-hand column holds the colour, not a title), so role_raw is empty for them. The grade-level headings are printed over the right NAME column (Grade 3 L17, Grade 4 L25, Grade 5 L32, Achieve/TLC L41) while the left column continues with staff, so those lines are counted as entry lines. L5-L8 are the School Council list (rule 7); role_raw drops only the trailing colon of the printed label ('Principal:', 'Teachers:', 'Parents:'). Norman Yvon and Bethann Cormier therefore appear twice on this page - once as council members (L5, L6) and once in the staff roster (L18, L19); Kate Robinson and Rhonda Connery likewise (L7 council, L36/L35 staff). Headings wrapped across lines and counted individually: L23+L24 'Nurse/Health &'+'Behavioral Health'; L38+L39+L40 'Learning'+'Center/Special'+'Education'. L17 prints '_Room#' (x=66) where a 'Title' column header would sit - recorded as printed, it is a heading line either way. L14-L15 are the narrative report's sign-off (Respectfully submitted, / Norman P. Yvon, Principal) and are ignored; Norman Yvon is captured from the roster and the council list."
